<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Italy</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Italy is a peninsula and country in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>. It was a battleground for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>, and later contested by the Byzantine, Carolingian, Holy Roman and Spanish empires. Unified in the nineteenth century, it built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a>, including its invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/italy.jpg" alt="Italy" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: See below. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Italy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
